When the same instance supplies demonstrations with widely different dimensions, background colors, seed colors, and motif shapes, do not assume the visible seed in the test is enough to derive a familiar operation. First record each pair's input/output changed-cell mask, foreground/background roles, and unchanged seed/background cells. Search for one role-level invariant that explains all pairs; explicitly reject candidate rules such as zero-component flood fill or global recoloring unless they reproduce every output exactly.

After each failed submission, revisit the transformation hypothesis rather than changing arbitrary thresholds or component definitions. If the demo cap is exhausted, use remaining submissions only for a rule supported by the full evidence. This instance's guesses of connected-background recoloring were not demonstrated by cross-pair replay and failed; the reusable lesson is to validate cross-demo invariance before committing, not to favor another particular rule.", "file_type": ".md", "_source_path": "/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-hermesagentlearner-1792545261/attempts/dc2dcdf57b4240ea8dfdb9832237f673/system/state/hermes/skills/reasoning/continual-arc-puzzle-solving/references/heterogeneous-demo-reconciliation.md"}

{"success": true, "name": "continual-arc-puzzle-solving", "file": "references/heterogeneous-demo-turn-selection.md", "content": "# Selecting demos for heterogeneous ARC examples

When available demonstrations differ sharply in grid size, palette, and object structure, log each pair's role colors, exact changed-cell mask, untouched/identity regions, and any plausible structural trigger. Treat a rule as supported only if it reproduces complete outputs, not merely the salient changed motif.

Before requesting another pair, name the competing hypotheses and the concrete observation that would distinguish them; ask only if that distinction can materially change the test prediction. Repeated requests without a targeted discriminator have cost but may not improve inference. In the same way, do not progress from one vivid example directly to a large speculative output: preserve the test input unless evidence supports a transformation. Keep this evidence-gathering discipline compatible with strict interfaces: each puzzle response still emits exactly one action JSON.", "file_type": ".md", "_source_path": "/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-hermesagentlearner-1792545261/attempts/dc2dcdf57b4240ea8dfdb9832237f673/system/state/hermes/skills/reasoning/continual-arc-puzzle-solving/references/heterogeneous-demo-turn-selection.md"}

{"success": true, "name": "continual-arc-puzzle-solving", "file": "references/stripe-demo-sparse-transfer-review.md", "content": "# Stripe demos with a structurally different test

In the reviewed instance, two demonstrations used uniform horizontal stripes and transformed them into full-grid periodic horizontal color sequences. The test was also uniform stripes, but only 7×7 with a different ordering/repetition of colors. The demos revealed periodic output behavior and some palette/sequence roles, but a speculative transfer to the test was not validated against a second demo matching the test's scale or pattern. The chosen test sequence was therefore underdetermined: cycle order, phase, and stripe-role selection needed to be distinguished instead of guessed.

For similar cases, tabulate input and output stripe colors row-by-row, preserve all repeated and untouched stripes in the comparison, and test a candidate role-level sequence rule against every demo. Separate palette/cycle inference from phase and trigger inference. A small or differently structured test should not automatically receive a rasterized version of the large demo's periodic sequence. Ask for another pair only if its stripe arrangement can discriminate specific candidate rules; otherwise submit only the strongest supported extrapolation and retain the strict one-action JSON protocol.", "file_type": ".md", "_source_path": "/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-hermesagentlearner-1792545261/attempts/dc2dcdf57b4240ea8dfdb9832237f673/system/state/hermes/skills/reasoning/continual-arc-puzzle-solving/references/stripe-demo-sparse-transfer-review.md"}

